[I] A multilingual input method framework

[T] Uim is a multilingual input method framework. It aims to provide a
[T] flexible development platform and useful user environment for input
[T] methods. It works in many environments, including general desktop
[T] systems such as GNOME or KDE, and even in a console. It also supports
[T] Linux Zaurus and Mac OS X.

[U] https://code.google.com/archive/p/uim/

[A] YamaKen <yamaken@bp.iij4u.or.jp>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/text
[F] CROSS FCOMMON

[E] opt dpkg

[L] BSD
[V] 2.0.0
[P] X -----5---9 200.000

[D] 4884b015aa38265717be6555b635b9add2f1d61b75beb328d16110f4 uim-2.0.0.tar.bz2 https://github.com/uim/uim/releases/download/2.0.0/

atstage cross && hook_add preconf 5 "echo 'ac_cv_func_realloc_0_nonnull=yes' >> config.cache"

atstage cross && var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' "-c?:-Wl,-rpath-link,$builddir/$pkg-$ver/uim/.libs:$builddir/$pkg-$ver/sigscheme/.libs:$builddir/$pkg-$ver/sigscheme/src/.libs:$builddir/$pkg-$ver/sigscheme/libgcroots/.libs"
